{
  "slug": "nail-sharding-in-system-design-interviews",
  "title": "Nail Sharding in System Design Interviews: Range-Based, Hash-Based, Directory-Based",
  "subtitle": "A Practical guide about Database Sharding and Partioning in System Design Interviews",
  "date": "2025-12-12",
  "canonical": "https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/p/nail-sharding-in-system-design-interviews",
  "body_html": "<p>Appreciate you reading this newsletter, I hope the content and resources are helping you level up as an engineer. If you want me to write about something specific, just message me or comment on the post.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Note:</strong> This article on was originally published on my blog -<strong> <a href=\"https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/sharding\">https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/sharding</a></strong></p></blockquote><p>Previously, we talked about how we deal with a situation when an application grows overnight more users, more traffic, more queries.<br>Our first reaction was straightforward:</p><ul><li><p>scale vertically (bigger machine),</p></li><li><p>scale horizontally (more servers for the app),</p></li><li><p>add read replicas to offload read traffic.</p></li></ul><p>And that worked… for reads.<strong><br></strong>You can read about it here - <a href=\"https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181087908/horizontal-scaling-sharding\">https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181087908/horizontal-scaling-sharding</a></p><p>Read replicas were amazing because they helped us spread the read load across multiple machines.<br>But there was <em>one thing</em> we still couldn’t scale: Writes.</p><p>No matter how many replicas we added, every single write still went to one place the primary database.</p><ul><li><p>All inserts? → Primary</p></li><li><p>All updates? → Primary</p></li><li><p>All deletes? → Primary</p></li></ul><p>And sure, we can increase CPU, add RAM, use faster disks…<br>But hardware scaling hits a limit.<br>Eventually, this one machine becomes the bottleneck for write heavy systems. </p><p>And that’s exactly where <strong>sharding</strong> comes in.</p><div><hr></div><h3>Sharding</h3><p>Split the data horizontally across multiple databases (shards), so writes are spread out instead of hitting a single node. So each shard now has its own CPU, its own memory, its own storage, its own connection pool.</p><p>A shard is just a subset of your data stored in a separate database.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png\" width=\"625\" height=\"398.35164835164835\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:928,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:625,&quot;bytes&quot;:846346,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181384498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!anq7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd3026946-c941-421d-9468-e1278e09d8cd_1726x1100.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><p>Example:</p><ul><li><p>Shard 1 → Users with IDs 1–1,000,000</p></li><li><p>Shard 2 → Users with IDs 1,000,001–2,000,000</p><p>As we grow we can increase the number of shards.</p></li></ul><p>You can (and usually should) have replication <em>inside</em> each shard:</p><ul><li><p>Shard 1 primary + read replicas</p></li><li><p>Shard 2 primary + read replicas<br>So you end up with: sharding for scaling writes, replication for High Availability + read scaling.</p></li></ul><p>So Sharding solves the problem of scalability in writes, but you may ask questions like: </p><ul><li><p>How does my request even know which shard to go to ? </p></li><li><p>What if one shard goes down </p></li><li><p>What if one shard receives most of the traffic?</p><div><hr></div></li></ul><h3>How to shard your data?</h3><p>When you decide to shard, you’re really making two decisions that work together:</p><ol><li><p>What to shard by (the shard key): This is the field/column you use to split the data – for example, <code>user_id</code>, <code>tenant_id</code>, or <code>country</code>. It defines how the data is logically grouped.</p></li><li><p>How to distribute it (the distribution strategy): This is the rule that assigns those groups to shards. It defines how those groups are spread across machines.</p></li></ol><p>In practice, this logic usually lives in your API/backend code as a routing strategy.<br>Every read or write request goes through this routing logic before it touches the database.</p><pre><code><code>// Pseudo-code in the API layer\n\nfunction getShardId(userId: number) {\n  // Simple hash-based strategy:\n  // use userId % 4 to pick one of 4 shards\n  return userId % 4;          // 0,1,2,3 → 4 shards\n}\n\nfunction getShardConnection(userId: number) {\n  const shardId = getShardId(userId);\n  return shardConnections[shardId];  // pick the right DB client\n}\n</code></code></pre><p>Here:</p><ul><li><p>Shard key = <code>userId</code></p></li><li><p>Distribution strategy = <code>userId % 4</code> (a simple hash-based rule)</p></li><li><p>Router = this bit of code that picks the correct DB connection</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div></li></ul><h3>Choosing the Right Shard Key ?  </h3><p>When you shard a database, the shard key decides how your data and traffic are split across machines. When you shard/partition data, you expect traffic to be spread out evenly.</p><p>A shard that receives disproportionately high traffic (reads or writes) compared to others, then it becomes a bottleneck while other shards sit mostly idle. This is called as hot partiotion. <br>Example:</p><ul><li><p>You shard by <code>country</code></p></li><li><p>60% of users are from <code>US</code></p></li><li><p>The <code>US</code> shard is overloaded = hot</p></li><li><p>Other shards (for smaller countries) are mostly idle = cold</p></li></ul><p>In that case, even if you have 10 shards, your system behaves like one overloaded shard.</p><p>So a good shard key should have: </p><ul><li><p><strong>High Cardinality</strong> </p><p>High cardinality makes it easier to avoid hot partitions, because the key space is nicely spread out.</p><ul><li><p>Good: <code>user_id</code>, <code>order_id</code>, <code>tenant_id</code></p></li><li><p>Bad: <code>country</code>, <code>plan_type</code>, <code>created_at</code> (only a few values → some shards get all traffic)</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Align with Query Patterns</strong></p><p>Your shard key should match how your application queries data.</p><ul><li><p>If most queries are <code>WHERE user_id = ?</code> → shard by <code>user_id</code></p></li><li><p>If you usually load “all data for a user” → that user’s data should live on one shard</p></li></ul><p>If your shard key has nothing to do with your query filters, you’ll end up with:</p><ul><li><p>Cross-shard queries</p></li><li><p>Distributed joins</p></li><li><p>Higher latency and complexity</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Immutable and Stable</strong></p><p>The shard key should never change after it’s chosen.</p><ul><li><p>Good: internal IDs (<code>user_id</code>, <code>tenant_id</code>)</p></li><li><p>Bad: <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>username</code>, <code>status</code></p></li></ul><p>If the shard key changes, you’d have to move rows across shards, which is slow, error-prone, and painful in production</p><div><hr></div></li></ul><h3>Different Sharding Strategies</h3><h4>1. Range Based Sharding </h4><p>Range-based sharding divides your data into contiguous ranges:</p><pre><code>Shard 1 → User IDs 1–1M\nShard 2 → User IDs 1M–2M\nShard 3 → User IDs 2M–3M</code></pre><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"794\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:794,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:4589439,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181384498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!6sBp!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F674844f8-2049-432b-a66d-1b0b7f38fa0d_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">range based sharding</figcaption></figure></div><p>The main advantage of range-based sharding is simplicity and support for efficient range scans. If you need all orders between user IDs 500K and 600K, you only hit one shard. </p><p>Range-based sharding is simple to implement and understand but it can lead to “hot spots,” where one shard is handling much more data than others. Early on, all traffic goes to the first range (because only low IDs exist), so one shard does all the work while the others are empty; later, as the system grows, all new writes and “recent activity” queries pile onto the latest range, so the last shard becomes the new hotspot.</p><h4>2. Hash Based Sharding </h4><p>Hash sharding uses a hash function to evenly distribute records across shards. Instead of assigning ranges, you take a shard key like user_id, hash it, and use the result to pick a shard. This is the default and most common sharding strategy.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"794\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/e21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:794,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:4923463,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181384498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Finu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe21c3b3f-cc7f-4247-8729-c5362656580d_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">hash based sharding</figcaption></figure></div><p>Hashing evenly distributes data across shards, minimizing hot spots.</p><p>Hash-based sharding using <code>hash(key) % N</code> spreads data evenly at first, but the moment you add or remove a shard, the value of <code>N</code> changes and almost every key now maps to a different shard, causing a massive reshuffle and painful rebalancing. Consistent hashing fixes this by placing shards and keys on a hash ring so that when the number of shards changes, only a small fraction of keys move to new shards, keeping the system much more stable and easier to scale.</p><p>We will talk about Consistent hashing in a different article. </p><h4>3. Directory Based Sharding </h4><p>Directory sharding uses a lookup table to decide where each record lives. Instead of using a formula, you store shard assignments in a mapping table or service.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png\" width=\"727\" height=\"396.4546703296703\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:794,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:727,&quot;bytes&quot;:4581453,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181384498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!m2zU!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F9db7b449-0079-4605-bf13-41032685ff47_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">directory based sharding</figcaption></figure></div><p>Directory-based sharding gives you maximum flexibility: you keep a mapping of <code>userId → shard</code>, so you can move heavy users to dedicated shards or rebalance load just by updating the directory instead of reshuffling all data. The tradeoff is that every request needs a directory lookup, which adds latency and turns the directory into a critical dependency if it goes down, your whole system is effectively down. </p><div><hr></div><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><h3>Partitioning</h3><p>Partitioning means splitting a large table into smaller pieces inside a single database instance.</p><p>Unlike sharding, partitioning doesn’t spread data across multiple machines. Instead, it helps organize data internally to speed up queries. Partitioning directly impacts performance and data manageability. Here are some of its key benefits:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Query optimization:</strong> Speeds up queries by limiting the search scope to a specific partition.</p></li><li><p><strong>Efficient data management:</strong> Simplifies data lifecycle management by segregating data for archiving or deletion.</p></li><li><p><strong>Better indexing and maintenance:</strong> Indexes can be applied at the partition level, reducing their size and making them easier to maintain. This keeps your database lean and responsive.</p></li></ul><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"794\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:794,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:4529163,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/181384498?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!fLXn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7089660b-e440-4f76-a544-49526f572932_2816x1536.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>There are 2 types of partitions : </p><h4>1. Horizontal Partitioning </h4><p>Split rows across partitions. For example split by row range.</p><h4>2. Vertical Partitioning</h4><p>Split columns across partitions. For example, keep frequently accessed columns in one partition and large or rarely used columns in another. Same rows, fewer columns per partition.</p><p>We’ve reached the end of this super informative blog.</p><p>Last but not the least to say that : </p><p>A scalable architecture almost always combines:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Sharding for write scalability</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Replication for HA + read scaling</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Partitioning for internal DB performance</strong></p></li></ul><p>Hope you liked this article, if you liked it then please do like and subscribe.It really motivates me to do better and make such amazing content. </p><p>Take Care and See you in the next one. </p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><